nullasblank_value: the builder reads only the words true and false, so the
SSL literal `.F.`, a number and a quoted "true" are all ignored and
null-to-blank stays on. Each value warns, ranged on the value. A real data
source holds one :NULLASBLANK; three lines here record that every
directive line is read. The `False` near miss is in
hybrid/header_only_stub.
-- input.ds --
:NULLASBLANK := .F.;
:NULLASBLANK := 0;
:NULLASBLANK := "true";
:PARAMETERS sMember := "";
SELECT member_code, phone FROM member WHERE member_code = @sMember
-- format --
:NULLASBLANK := .F.;
:NULLASBLANK := 0;
:NULLASBLANK := "true";
:PARAMETERS sMember := "";
SELECT member_code, phone FROM member WHERE member_code = @sMember
-- diagnostics --
1:17-1:20 warning nullasblank_value: ':NULLASBLANK' takes the word true or false; any other value is ignored and null-to-blank stays on
2:17-2:18 warning nullasblank_value: ':NULLASBLANK' takes the word true or false; any other value is ignored and null-to-blank stays on
3:17-3:23 warning nullasblank_value: ':NULLASBLANK' takes the word true or false; any other value is ignored and null-to-blank stays on
